<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot pork 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot pork 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compared to Thursday's 3:00 PM close, fresh loins were 4.00 higher in a light test; butts were not tested; skinned hams 17-20 lbs were 2.00-3.00 higher, 20-26 lbs 3.00 higher; seedless bellies were 2.00-3.00 higher; lean trimmings were steady to 1.00 higher, USDA said. Trading was slow,with moderate demand and very light to light offerings.</p>
<p>NOTE: 0.5 LD of 4-8 lb butt traded at $71.00.</p>
